  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a tree with NNN nodes (numbered 111 through NNN). For each valid iii, node iii has a value AiA_iAi​.\n\nYou should answer QQQ queries. In each query:\n\n\nYou are given two nodes aaa and bbb.\nLet SSS denote the set of all nodes on the simple path between the nodes aaa and bbb (including these nodes).\nFind the minimum value of ∣Ax−Ay∣|A_x-A_y|∣Ax​−Ay​∣ over all pairs x,y∈Sx, y \\in Sx,y∈S such that x≠yx \\neq yx=y.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤201 \\le T \\le 201≤T≤20",
      "2≤N≤2⋅1052 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^52≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Q≤2⋅1051 \\le Q \\le 2 \\cdot 10^51≤Q≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Ai≤1001 \\le A_i \\le 1001≤Ai​≤100 for each valid iii",
      "1≤u,v,a,b≤N1 \\le u, v, a, b \\le N1≤u,v,a,b≤N",
      "a≠ba \\neq ba=b",
      "the sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 5⋅1055 \\cdot 10^55⋅105",
      "the sum of QQQ over all test cases does not exceed 5⋅1055 \\cdot 10^55⋅105",
      "Subtasks**Subtask #1 (30 points):** N,Q≤1,000N, Q \\le 1,000N,Q≤1,000"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and QQQ.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\nEach of the next N−1N-1N−1 lines contains two space-separated integers uuu and vvv denoting that nodes uuu and vvv are connected by an edge.\nEach of the last QQQ lines contains two space-separated integers aaa and bbb describing a query.",
    "outputFormat": "For each query, print a single line containing one integer ― the answer to the query.",
    "notes": [],
